# Copy to a private file named `.env` in the repository root, then fill it in.
# `astro_launcher.bash` sources this file; it is the ONLY consumer.
#
# SECURITY: `.env` is git-ignored. Never commit a real key. Rotate any key that
# is ever committed, shared, or pasted into a bug report.
#
# The `astroom` application itself reads NO environment variables. Every setting
# reaches it through explicit CLI flags. If you prefer not to use the launcher,
# pass the key directly:
#     ./target/release/astroom run-pipeline --api-key "<YOUR_KEY>" ...
# or read it from a file (0600) and use:
#     ./target/release/astroom run-pipeline --api-key-file /path/to/key ...
#
# OpenRouter (or any OpenAI-compatible) API key. Required for the LLM stages
# (jobCloth, remoteEval, jobJudge, makeMaterials). The shipped presets in
# config/presets.json all target OpenRouter.
AOM_OR_API_KEY=

# Optional Indeed scraper credential. Not required: `astroom` falls back to the
# public Indeed mobile client key compiled into the binary. Set this only if you
# have your own Indeed API key.
# AOM_INDEED_API_KEY=

# Optional explicit directory redirection (forwarded as --data-dir etc.).
# Relative paths are resolved from your current working directory.
# AOM_DATA_DIR=./data
# AOM_LOG_DIR=./logs
# AOM_MATERIALS_DIR=./materials
# AOM_PROFILE_DIR=./profile

# Optional launcher behavior (forwarded as --clean / --deploy flags).
# AOM_CLEAN=1
# AOM_DEPLOY=1

# Required when AOM_DEPLOY=1. Any rclone remote or local path.
# AOM_DEPLOY_DESTINATION="GoogleDrive:/my-astroom-output"
